<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matthias, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1557">1557</a>–<a href="/years/1619">1619</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matthias was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> from 1612 to 1619 and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, a son of Emperor Maximilian II. As archduke he challenged his brother Rudolf II and in 1608, backed by the estates of Hungary, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, forced Rudolf to cede him those lands. His reign ended amid the Bohemian revolt that began <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matthias-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Matthias, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas van Valckenborch · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucas_van_Valckenborch_-_Emperor_Matthias_as_Archduke,_with_baton.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
